# Agent tooling — ignore local/transient state under the generated trees; keep
# rulesync outputs (and optional shared Cursor hooks) trackable. New junk from
# Cursor / Claude Code / Codex is ignored by default. Un-ignore both the
# directory and its contents (`!dir/` + `!dir/**`) so nested files are not
# blocked by the parent `.cursor/*` / `.claude/*` / `.agents/*` exclude.
#
# Keep trackable (rulesync):
#   .cursor/{rules,commands,skills,hooks.json}/
#   .claude/{rules,commands,skills,settings.json}/
#   .agents/{memories,skills}/
#   .codex/hooks.json
# Stay local (examples): .cursor/debug.log, .cursor/plans/, .cursor/mcp.json,
#   .claude/settings.local.json, .claude/worktrees/, .claude/agent-memory-local/
.cursor/*
!.cursor/rules/
!.cursor/rules/**
!.cursor/commands/
!.cursor/commands/**
!.cursor/skills/
!.cursor/skills/**
!.cursor/hooks.json
!.cursor/hooks/
!.cursor/hooks/**

.claude/*
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/rules/**
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/commands/**
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks.json
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/hooks/**

.agents/*
!.agents/memories/
!.agents/memories/**
!.agents/skills/
!.agents/skills/**

.codex/*
!.codex/hooks.json

# Root-level personal overrides (Claude Code + Codex) — never commit
CLAUDE.local.md
**/AGENTS.override.md

# RuleSync verifies these restored npm-source caches against the committed
# rulesync-npm.lock.json. They are installation artifacts; generated target
# rules remain committed and reviewable.
.rulesync/**/.curated/
